WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.800
Hi, I'm Nei Maldaner,

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.060
and this is module seven of

3
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:04.820
OSWork.

4
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.100
In the last module,

5
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.640
you learned to save versions of your

6
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.780
work with Git,

7
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.800
so nothing gets lost.

8
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:11.960
Now we're going to find a way

9
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.200
to talk to a program of yours

10
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.260
from your phone,

11
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:15.280
using Telegram.

12
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.600
By the end of this module,

13
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.720
you'll have a bot of your own,

14
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.520
created on Telegram,

15
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.400
with its key kept

16
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.840
in a place nobody sees,

17
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.100
serving only the people you've authorized,

18
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.300
and

19
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.420
answering two lookup commands without executing any

20
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.260
message.

21
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.080
You'll also know where an AI could

22
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.860
come in without messing up the numbers,

23
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.980
and how to test everything before you

24
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.480
trust it.

25
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.320
Denise and Lúcia are still with us:

26
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.760
Lúcia is going to build a bot

27
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.540
for the grêmio's fictional school shop.

28
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.600
Each lesson has a short practice.

29
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.500
When I ask,

30
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.840
pause the video and do it right

31
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:49.340
then.

32
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.980
Let's start by separating two things that

33
00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.380
usually get mixed up.

34
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.480
When you chat with a bot on

35
00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.460
Telegram, the app on your phone only

36
00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.460
carries your message and brings the reply

37
00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:57.960
back.

38
00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.460
The one that reads,

39
00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.440
decides and replies is a program running

40
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.280
on your computer.

41
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.460
Think of the intercom at the gatehouse:

42
00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.269
the device carries the voice,

43
00:01:06.269 --> 00:01:08.069
but the person inside is the one

44
00:01:08.069 --> 00:01:09.589
who opens the gate.

45
00:01:09.589 --> 00:01:11.129
Denise heard that another school had an

46
00:01:11.129 --> 00:01:12.569
agent on Telegram.

47
00:01:12.569 --> 00:01:14.349
She asked what it did and found

48
00:01:14.349 --> 00:01:16.129
out it was three canned replies,

49
00:01:16.129 --> 00:01:18.689
with no AI at all.

50
00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:19.929
The name promised more than the thing

51
00:01:19.929 --> 00:01:20.809
delivered.

52
00:01:20.809 --> 00:01:23.009
So keep this division in mind:

53
00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:25.329
Telegram receives what you write and delivers

54
00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:27.109
the reply in the same chat.

55
00:01:27.109 --> 00:01:29.389
Your program checks who wrote and which

56
00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.889
command it is,

57
00:01:30.889 --> 00:01:31.969
executes

58
00:01:31.969 --> 00:01:33.889
only the allowed function,

59
00:01:33.889 --> 00:01:35.309
and builds the reply.

60
00:01:35.309 --> 00:01:36.649
Both parts are needed,

61
00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:38.409
but only one decides.

62
00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:40.169
The bot in the course kit has

63
00:01:40.169 --> 00:01:41.009
two work commands,

64
00:01:41.009 --> 00:01:42.909
and neither uses AI.

65
00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:45.889
The status command confirms it's running.

66
00:01:45.989 --> 00:01:47.069
The relatorio command,

67
00:01:47.069 --> 00:01:49.109
which means report,

68
00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.029
adds up three fictional sales from a

69
00:01:52.029 --> 00:01:54.229
file called vendas dot CSV,

70
00:01:54.229 --> 00:01:56.469
a spreadsheet in plain text.

71
00:01:56.469 --> 00:01:58.949
Lúcia will use this bot to check

72
00:01:58.949 --> 00:02:00.369
on the grêmio's shop:

73
00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:02.509
notebook, pen and planner.

74
00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:03.429
She sends relatorio,

75
00:02:03.429 --> 00:02:05.129
and the bot replies that there were

76
00:02:05.129 --> 00:02:07.509
three sales, totaling one hundred reais.

77
00:02:07.509 --> 00:02:09.769
That total comes from a calculation the

78
00:02:09.769 --> 00:02:10.949
program makes,

79
00:02:10.949 --> 00:02:12.559
not from a guess.

80
00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.619
That's what deterministic means:

81
00:02:14.619 --> 00:02:16.959
the same request always gets the same

82
00:02:16.959 --> 00:02:18.159
reply.

83
00:02:18.279 --> 00:02:20.359
And there's one more important detail.

84
00:02:20.359 --> 00:02:22.359
Whoever writes on Telegram doesn't control the

85
00:02:22.359 --> 00:02:23.319
computer.

86
00:02:23.319 --> 00:02:25.459
The bot compares the message with

87
00:02:25.459 --> 00:02:27.979
a short list of known commands,

88
00:02:27.999 --> 00:02:30.179
and everything else gets the same standard

89
00:02:30.179 --> 00:02:31.199
reply:

90
00:02:31.199 --> 00:02:31.699
unknown command.

91
00:02:31.559 --> 00:02:32.559
That

92
00:02:32.559 --> 00:02:34.699
goes even for the bot's owner.

93
00:02:34.699 --> 00:02:37.639
Denise imagined a school office bot that

94
00:02:37.639 --> 00:02:39.379
received the sentence,

95
00:02:39.839 --> 00:02:42.079
delete yesterday's absences.

96
00:02:42.139 --> 00:02:44.139
With a closed list of commands,

97
00:02:44.139 --> 00:02:46.539
that sentence comes back as unknown command,

98
00:02:46.539 --> 00:02:48.499
and nothing is deleted.

99
00:02:48.499 --> 00:02:50.979
That's why, before you think about AI,

100
00:02:50.979 --> 00:02:52.539
you draw the whole path of a

101
00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:53.399
message.

102
00:02:53.399 --> 00:02:54.799
Then you mark the step where it

103
00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:56.019
would really help.

104
00:02:56.019 --> 00:02:57.859
A good candidate is the function:

105
00:02:57.859 --> 00:02:59.519
it could gain a text summary built

106
00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:00.699
from the numbers.

107
00:03:00.699 --> 00:03:01.619
The rule is firm:

108
00:03:01.619 --> 00:03:05.219
the number stays the program's number.

109
00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:08.019
Lúcia marked that step.

110
00:03:08.019 --> 00:03:10.059
The AI could write that the planner

111
00:03:10.059 --> 00:03:11.299
was the biggest sale,

112
00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:12.879
as long as the one hundred reais

113
00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:15.779
total stays exactly as the program calculated

114
00:03:15.779 --> 00:03:16.399
it.

115
00:03:16.399 --> 00:03:17.728
Now pause the video.

116
00:03:17.728 --> 00:03:18.928
On paper,

117
00:03:18.928 --> 00:03:20.228
draw five

118
00:03:20.288 --> 00:03:21.628
boxes in a row:

119
00:03:21.628 --> 00:03:23.928
phone, Telegram, bot,

120
00:03:23.928 --> 00:03:25.828
allowed function and reply.

121
00:03:25.828 --> 00:03:26.988
Under each one,

122
00:03:26.988 --> 00:03:28.748
write who does the work.

123
00:03:28.748 --> 00:03:30.108
Put an X in a single box

124
00:03:30.108 --> 00:03:32.508
and write what the AI would do

125
00:03:32.508 --> 00:03:34.348
there, without changing numbers.

126
00:03:34.348 --> 00:03:36.348
Every Telegram bot is born in a

127
00:03:36.348 --> 00:03:37.848
chat with BotFather.

128
00:03:37.848 --> 00:03:39.548
You send the newbot command,

129
00:03:39.548 --> 00:03:40.768
choose a name and a username,

130
00:03:40.768 --> 00:03:42.128
and it gives you back the bot's

131
00:03:42.128 --> 00:03:42.908
token.

132
00:03:42.908 --> 00:03:44.888
The username has to end in bot,

133
00:03:44.888 --> 00:03:47.288
like lojinha gremio lucia bot,

134
00:03:47.288 --> 00:03:49.128
and if it's already taken,

135
00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.108
BotFather asks for another one.

136
00:03:51.108 --> 00:03:52.808
The token is a string of numbers,

137
00:03:52.808 --> 00:03:54.308
a colon and letters.

138
00:03:54.308 --> 00:03:55.428
It works like the key to the

139
00:03:55.428 --> 00:03:56.408
school gate:

140
00:03:56.408 --> 00:03:58.468
whoever has a copy gets in,

141
00:03:58.468 --> 00:03:59.908
whoever they are.

142
00:03:59.908 --> 00:04:01.528
Lúcia created the shop bot in three

143
00:04:01.528 --> 00:04:02.348
messages.

144
00:04:02.348 --> 00:04:04.388
But first, she checked something important:

145
00:04:04.388 --> 00:04:06.188
that she was talking to the official

146
00:04:06.188 --> 00:04:07.828
BotFather, with

147
00:04:07.948 --> 00:04:09.428
the blue verified badge,

148
00:04:09.428 --> 00:04:11.868
and not to an account with a

149
00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:13.328
similar name.

150
00:04:13.368 --> 00:04:14.908
A practical detail:

151
00:04:14.908 --> 00:04:16.988
BotFather replies in English.

152
00:04:16.988 --> 00:04:17.768
And notice that,

153
00:04:17.768 --> 00:04:18.788
in the lesson,

154
00:04:18.788 --> 00:04:20.868
the token is hidden on purpose.

155
00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.228
That's the same care you're going to

156
00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.268
take with yours.

157
00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.520
Where do you keep that key?

158
00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.600
In the bot folder,

159
00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.007
the course kit includes an example file,

160
00:04:29.007 --> 00:04:30.620
dot env dot example,

161
00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.840
with only fake values.

162
00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.880
You make a copy called dot env

163
00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:37.620
and paste the token inside it.

164
00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.340
That file stays on your computer only.

165
00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.260
The

166
00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.540
token doesn't go into a screenshot,

167
00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:45.320
a message, or a shared document.

168
00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:46.960
Denise thought about putting the token in

169
00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.580
the school office's instructions document,

170
00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.700
so nobody would lose it.

171
00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.420
She changed her mind:

172
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.440
the document says where the file is,

173
00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.120
never the value.

174
00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:57.940
In the terminal,

175
00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.460
inside the kit's bot folder,

176
00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:00.800
it's four commands:

177
00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.220
go into the folder,

178
00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:03.440
copy the example,

179
00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.900
restrict reading with chmod six hundred,

180
00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.340
and check with ls.

181
00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.600
Chmod six hundred lets only your account

182
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.680
read and change the file.

183
00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.660
The last line has to start with

184
00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.760
dash, r, w,

185
00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.600
and then only dashes.

186
00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.400
The first three commands show nothing when

187
00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.680
they work, and that's normal.

188
00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.500
If you get a message that the

189
00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.140
file doesn't exist,

190
00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.160
you're not in the right folder:

191
00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.380
repeat the cd command with the path

192
00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.280
where you unzipped the kit.

193
00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:30.480
And if the token shows up in

194
00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.420
a screenshot, a message or a document,

195
00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:34.265
treat it as leaked.

196
00:05:34.265 --> 00:05:36.845
In BotFather, send mybots,

197
00:05:36.845 --> 00:05:37.845
pick the bot,

198
00:05:37.845 --> 00:05:40.965
tap API Token and then Revoke current

199
00:05:40.965 --> 00:05:41.565
token.

200
00:05:41.565 --> 00:05:43.205
It generates a new token,

201
00:05:43.205 --> 00:05:45.425
and the old one stops working.

202
00:05:45.425 --> 00:05:47.655
Then replace the value in the dot

203
00:05:47.655 --> 00:05:48.155
env.

204
00:05:47.865 --> 00:05:49.165
In a meeting,

205
00:05:49.165 --> 00:05:51.165
Denise saw a colleague's screenshot with the

206
00:05:51.165 --> 00:05:52.705
token in plain view.

207
00:05:52.705 --> 00:05:54.045
She spoke up right away,

208
00:05:54.045 --> 00:05:56.145
and the team revoked and replaced it

209
00:05:56.145 --> 00:05:57.025
in ten minutes.

210
00:05:57.025 --> 00:05:58.785
Now pause the video.

211
00:05:58.785 --> 00:06:00.105
Create your bot in BotFather,

212
00:06:00.105 --> 00:06:01.645
run the four commands,

213
00:06:01.645 --> 00:06:03.305
check the permissions line and,

214
00:06:03.305 --> 00:06:06.285
with the command nano dot env,

215
00:06:06.285 --> 00:06:08.655
replace the placeholder text

216
00:06:08.655 --> 00:06:11.005
preencha localmente with your token.

217
00:06:11.005 --> 00:06:12.885
No screenshots.

218
00:06:12.965 --> 00:06:14.665
With the token stored,

219
00:06:14.985 --> 00:06:16.165
another question comes up:

220
00:06:16.165 --> 00:06:18.605
who can talk to the bot?

221
00:06:18.605 --> 00:06:20.165
The token proves to Telegram that your

222
00:06:20.165 --> 00:06:21.285
program owns the bot,

223
00:06:21.285 --> 00:06:22.865
but it says nothing about who can

224
00:06:22.865 --> 00:06:23.405
talk to it.

225
00:06:23.405 --> 00:06:25.405
That's why the kit has a second

226
00:06:25.405 --> 00:06:26.325
control,

227
00:06:26.325 --> 00:06:26.905
the access list.

228
00:06:26.905 --> 00:06:29.105
It's like the list of who can

229
00:06:29.105 --> 00:06:30.825
pick up each student at the end

230
00:06:30.825 --> 00:06:32.505
of the school day.

231
00:06:32.865 --> 00:06:34.525
Denise explained it to the team this

232
00:06:34.525 --> 00:06:36.505
way: the key opens the gate,

233
00:06:36.505 --> 00:06:38.985
and the pickup list says who takes

234
00:06:38.985 --> 00:06:40.265
each student home.

235
00:06:40.265 --> 00:06:41.365
They're two separate checks,

236
00:06:41.365 --> 00:06:44.385
and one doesn't replace the other.

237
00:06:44.385 --> 00:06:47.005
Both live in the same dot env

238
00:06:47.005 --> 00:06:47.991
file:

239
00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:49.911
the token on the TELEGRAM BOT TOKEN

240
00:06:49.911 --> 00:06:51.791
line, and the list on the ALLOWED

241
00:06:51.791 --> 00:06:53.551
USER IDS line.

242
00:06:53.551 --> 00:06:55.831
And that list doesn't

243
00:06:55.911 --> 00:06:56.791
store names.

244
00:06:56.791 --> 00:06:58.311
The name that shows up in the

245
00:06:58.311 --> 00:07:00.971
chat, a person can change whenever they

246
00:07:00.971 --> 00:07:01.951
want.

247
00:07:01.951 --> 00:07:04.051
The bot checks the numeric ID,

248
00:07:04.051 --> 00:07:07.091
the number Telegram gives each account.

249
00:07:07.931 --> 00:07:10.871
Lúcia shows up on Telegram as

250
00:07:10.871 --> 00:07:11.591
Lúcia Ciências.

251
00:07:11.591 --> 00:07:12.631
If

252
00:07:12.631 --> 00:07:14.591
she changes it to

253
00:07:14.951 --> 00:07:15.451
Prof.

254
00:07:15.171 --> 00:07:16.371
Lúcia,

255
00:07:16.471 --> 00:07:18.451
the bot still recognizes her,

256
00:07:18.451 --> 00:07:20.911
because her number is the same.

257
00:07:20.911 --> 00:07:22.091
To find your number,

258
00:07:22.091 --> 00:07:23.911
the kit has an identification-only

259
00:07:23.911 --> 00:07:24.871
mode:

260
00:07:24.871 --> 00:07:25.971
the command

261
00:07:25.971 --> 00:07:29.291
python3 bot.py with the identify option.

262
00:07:29.291 --> 00:07:30.091
In this mode,

263
00:07:30.091 --> 00:07:31.711
the bot doesn't reply to anything on

264
00:07:31.711 --> 00:07:33.971
your phone, and doesn't execute any function.

265
00:07:33.971 --> 00:07:34.911
You

266
00:07:34.911 --> 00:07:36.871
send the start command in a private

267
00:07:36.871 --> 00:07:38.171
chat with the bot,

268
00:07:38.171 --> 00:07:39.751
and the number shows up in the

269
00:07:39.751 --> 00:07:42.231
terminal, on a line that says ID

270
00:07:42.231 --> 00:07:43.991
recebido, ID received.

271
00:07:43.991 --> 00:07:46.391
Then you copy the number and stop

272
00:07:46.391 --> 00:07:47.411
it with Ctrl C.

273
00:07:47.411 --> 00:07:48.771
The number you see here on screen

274
00:07:48.771 --> 00:07:50.431
is fictional;

275
00:07:50.431 --> 00:07:51.871
yours will be different.

276
00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:54.871
If the terminal doesn't show any number,

277
00:07:55.091 --> 00:07:56.111
check three things:

278
00:07:56.111 --> 00:07:58.836
that you sent start in a private

279
00:07:58.836 --> 00:08:00.796
chat, not in a group;

280
00:08:00.796 --> 00:08:03.316
that the token in the dot env

281
00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:06.036
belongs to the right bot;

282
00:08:06.036 --> 00:08:08.596
and that identification mode was

283
00:08:08.596 --> 00:08:09.716
still running.

284
00:08:09.716 --> 00:08:12.156
Before replying, the program checks three things,

285
00:08:12.156 --> 00:08:13.956
in this order.

286
00:08:14.276 --> 00:08:15.576
Is it a private chat?

287
00:08:15.576 --> 00:08:16.676
If it's a group,

288
00:08:16.676 --> 00:08:17.756
silence.

289
00:08:17.756 --> 00:08:19.456
Is the ID on the access list?

290
00:08:19.456 --> 00:08:21.236
If not, silence.

291
00:08:21.236 --> 00:08:23.756
Is the command status or relatorio?

292
00:08:23.756 --> 00:08:25.856
If it's any other text,

293
00:08:25.856 --> 00:08:29.216
the only reply is unknown command.

294
00:08:29.756 --> 00:08:32.496
And only then does it execute that

295
00:08:32.496 --> 00:08:34.196
command's function.

296
00:08:34.276 --> 00:08:36.896
Denise wanted to test Lúcia's bot,

297
00:08:36.896 --> 00:08:38.316
sent relatorio

298
00:08:38.356 --> 00:08:39.736
and got nothing back.

299
00:08:39.736 --> 00:08:41.076
It wasn't a bug:

300
00:08:41.076 --> 00:08:43.116
her number wasn't on the list.

301
00:08:43.116 --> 00:08:44.216
With your number in hand,

302
00:08:44.216 --> 00:08:46.556
open the dot env and

303
00:08:46.556 --> 00:08:48.964
replace one two three four five six

304
00:08:48.964 --> 00:08:49.756
seven eight nine,

305
00:08:49.756 --> 00:08:51.756
which is just the kit's example,

306
00:08:51.756 --> 00:08:52.316
with your ID.

307
00:08:52.316 --> 00:08:53.836
For more people,

308
00:08:53.836 --> 00:08:56.436
separate the numbers with commas,

309
00:08:56.436 --> 00:08:58.216
but start with just yourself.

310
00:08:58.216 --> 00:09:00.156
Pause the video:

311
00:09:00.156 --> 00:09:02.966
check that python3 is version three point

312
00:09:02.966 --> 00:09:04.276
ten or higher,

313
00:09:04.276 --> 00:09:06.136
run identification mode,

314
00:09:06.136 --> 00:09:07.796
write down your number and put it

315
00:09:07.796 --> 00:09:08.461
on the list.

316
00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:09.980
With the list ready,

317
00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:12.000
how does the bot keep listening?

318
00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.320
With long polling,

319
00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.080
the program asks Telegram whether a new

320
00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:16.600
message has arrived.

321
00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.440
If not, it waits up to twenty-five

322
00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.040
seconds and asks again.

323
00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.280
It's like stopping by your cubby in

324
00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:22.900
the teachers' room and lingering for a

325
00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:25.400
moment, in case a note shows up.

326
00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.320
There's another way,

327
00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:28.080
the webhook, which would be the mail

328
00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.140
carrier ringing the doorbell:

329
00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:31.680
Telegram calls an address of yours on

330
00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.180
the internet.

331
00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:34.880
But that requires a public address,

332
00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:37.240
and it isn't used in this module.

333
00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:38.440
Both work,

334
00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.500
but the kit uses the first one.

335
00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.060
Lúcia left the bot running on her

336
00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.000
laptop,

337
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.840
at home, and didn't have to touch

338
00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.540
any network settings.

339
00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:47.800
The program goes out to fetch the

340
00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:49.800
messages, and nobody needs to get into

341
00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.100
her computer.

342
00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:52.060
To start it,

343
00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.460
in the terminal,

344
00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:54.740
in the bot folder,

345
00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.300
run python3 bot.py.

346
00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:57.600
No line appears,

347
00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:58.240
and that's the right sign:

348
00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.420
the program is waiting.

349
00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:02.740
The terminal has to stay open.

350
00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.620
Close the window or press Ctrl C,

351
00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.720
and the bot stops replying.

352
00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.940
Denise found the still screen strange and

353
00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:10.260
almost closed it.

354
00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.800
Lúcia explained:

355
00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:14.620
a screen with no new lines is

356
00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:15.866
the bot working,

357
00:10:15.866 --> 00:10:17.466
and a new line is usually a

358
00:10:17.466 --> 00:10:18.506
warning.

359
00:10:18.506 --> 00:10:19.766
With the bot running,

360
00:10:19.766 --> 00:10:22.166
send status and relatorio in the private

361
00:10:22.166 --> 00:10:22.926
chat.

362
00:10:22.926 --> 00:10:24.406
But before you start it,

363
00:10:24.406 --> 00:10:25.986
look at the file with the command

364
00:10:25.986 --> 00:10:27.746
cat vendas.csv,

365
00:10:28.986 --> 00:10:31.546
because afterwards the terminal is busy.

366
00:10:31.546 --> 00:10:33.899
Lúcia added it up on paper:

367
00:10:33.899 --> 00:10:35.546
thirty-five fifty, plus

368
00:10:35.546 --> 00:10:36.976
nine fifty, plus

369
00:10:36.976 --> 00:10:37.526
fifty-five.

370
00:10:37.526 --> 00:10:39.106
That came to one hundred reais,

371
00:10:39.106 --> 00:10:41.426
the same number as the bot.

372
00:10:41.426 --> 00:10:43.406
A total that matches the file is

373
00:10:43.406 --> 00:10:44.906
a verified result,

374
00:10:44.906 --> 00:10:46.466
not an impression.

375
00:10:46.526 --> 00:10:48.066
One more precaution:

376
00:10:48.166 --> 00:10:50.346
keep a single program fetching messages for

377
00:10:50.346 --> 00:10:51.406
each bot.

378
00:10:51.406 --> 00:10:53.266
Two at the same time,

379
00:10:53.526 --> 00:10:54.786
with the same token,

380
00:10:54.786 --> 00:10:55.866
compete for the messages,

381
00:10:55.866 --> 00:10:57.966
and Telegram refuses.

382
00:10:57.966 --> 00:11:00.106
The kit notices that conflict and

383
00:11:00.106 --> 00:11:01.126
shuts itself down,

384
00:11:01.126 --> 00:11:02.606
with a warning in the log,

385
00:11:02.606 --> 00:11:04.606
which shows up right in the terminal

386
00:11:04.606 --> 00:11:06.486
without revealing the token.

387
00:11:06.486 --> 00:11:08.486
The warning number is four oh nine,

388
00:11:08.486 --> 00:11:10.546
which means conflict.

389
00:11:10.966 --> 00:11:12.526
Lúcia started the bot at home,

390
00:11:12.526 --> 00:11:14.166
forgetting it was still running on the

391
00:11:14.166 --> 00:11:15.926
school laptop, and the one at home

392
00:11:15.926 --> 00:11:17.166
stopped with that warning.

393
00:11:17.166 --> 00:11:18.286
The next day,

394
00:11:18.286 --> 00:11:19.486
she stopped the one at school and

395
00:11:19.486 --> 00:11:21.511
restarted the one at home.

396
00:11:21.511 --> 00:11:23.571
Now pause the video.

397
00:11:23.571 --> 00:11:25.511
Add up the sales file on paper,

398
00:11:25.511 --> 00:11:26.871
start the bot,

399
00:11:26.871 --> 00:11:29.251
send status and relatorio from your phone,

400
00:11:29.251 --> 00:11:30.731
and compare the total.

401
00:11:30.731 --> 00:11:33.771
Then press Ctrl C and

402
00:11:33.771 --> 00:11:34.831
send status again:

403
00:11:34.831 --> 00:11:37.471
no reply should come.

404
00:11:37.591 --> 00:11:38.891
If the bot replies later,

405
00:11:38.891 --> 00:11:39.951
when you restart it,

406
00:11:39.951 --> 00:11:41.051
that's normal.

407
00:11:41.051 --> 00:11:43.431
The bot works without AI.

408
00:11:43.431 --> 00:11:45.871
So where would AI come in without

409
00:11:45.871 --> 00:11:47.311
spoiling the total?

410
00:11:47.311 --> 00:11:50.231
The kit deliberately separates the message path,

411
00:11:50.231 --> 00:11:51.671
which is Telegram,

412
00:11:51.671 --> 00:11:53.011
from the work functions.

413
00:11:53.011 --> 00:11:55.211
And it starts with no AI:

414
00:11:55.211 --> 00:11:58.271
status and a report on fictional data.

415
00:11:58.271 --> 00:12:00.011
A predictable bot is one you can

416
00:12:00.011 --> 00:12:02.091
test without spending anything.

417
00:12:02.091 --> 00:12:03.831
Only then is

418
00:12:03.931 --> 00:12:07.331
it worth asking whether AI improves interpretation,

419
00:12:07.851 --> 00:12:08.791
summarizing

420
00:12:08.791 --> 00:12:10.131
or classification.

421
00:12:10.371 --> 00:12:13.051
Denise wanted a school office

422
00:12:13.051 --> 00:12:15.831
FAQ bot with AI from the start.

423
00:12:15.831 --> 00:12:17.551
She changed the plan:

424
00:12:17.551 --> 00:12:19.571
first a horario command,

425
00:12:19.571 --> 00:12:22.011
for schedules, that only reads the spreadsheet,

426
00:12:22.011 --> 00:12:23.811
and the AI was left for a

427
00:12:23.811 --> 00:12:25.651
second step, with testing.

428
00:12:25.731 --> 00:12:27.331
If a new bot already calls an

429
00:12:27.331 --> 00:12:28.851
AI for

430
00:12:29.177 --> 00:12:30.377
everything,

431
00:12:30.557 --> 00:12:32.817
when it gets something wrong nobody knows

432
00:12:32.817 --> 00:12:35.057
whether it was the program or the

433
00:12:35.057 --> 00:12:36.177
AI.

434
00:12:36.177 --> 00:12:37.297
Step by step,

435
00:12:37.297 --> 00:12:39.477
step two is compared with the result

436
00:12:39.477 --> 00:12:40.097
of step one,

437
00:12:40.097 --> 00:12:42.637
and you investigate one error at a

438
00:12:42.637 --> 00:12:43.277
time.

439
00:12:43.277 --> 00:12:44.997
On a report card,

440
00:12:45.217 --> 00:12:47.037
the grade comes from the calculation,

441
00:12:47.037 --> 00:12:50.057
and the written comment discusses it.

442
00:12:50.057 --> 00:12:52.351
The comment never changes

443
00:12:52.351 --> 00:12:53.137
the grade.

444
00:12:53.137 --> 00:12:54.697
It's the same with the bot:

445
00:12:54.697 --> 00:12:56.257
the AI can write a summary,

446
00:12:56.257 --> 00:12:58.117
but the total comes from the program

447
00:12:58.117 --> 00:13:00.217
and can't change in the text.

448
00:13:00.217 --> 00:13:02.637
Lúcia imagined a resumo command,

449
00:13:02.637 --> 00:13:04.217
a summary, for the shop.

450
00:13:04.217 --> 00:13:06.237
The AI would receive only the total

451
00:13:06.237 --> 00:13:07.697
and the three products,

452
00:13:07.697 --> 00:13:10.117
not the entire folder of her projects.

453
00:13:10.117 --> 00:13:11.657
Look at what happened in the chat.

454
00:13:11.657 --> 00:13:13.417
Given the data and a request for

455
00:13:13.417 --> 00:13:14.617
a two-line summary,

456
00:13:14.617 --> 00:13:16.537
the AI wrote that sales added up

457
00:13:16.537 --> 00:13:18.357
to about one hundred and ten reais.

458
00:13:18.357 --> 00:13:19.557
It

459
00:13:19.577 --> 00:13:21.937
made up a total that doesn't exist,

460
00:13:21.937 --> 00:13:23.417
and that text can't go out through

461
00:13:23.417 --> 00:13:24.217
the bot.

462
00:13:24.217 --> 00:13:25.357
With the sentence

463
00:13:25.357 --> 00:13:27.057
use only this data,

464
00:13:27.057 --> 00:13:28.657
don't change any number and don't add

465
00:13:28.657 --> 00:13:30.911
data, the total came back as one

466
00:13:30.911 --> 00:13:32.257
hundred reais,

467
00:13:32.317 --> 00:13:33.717
with the planner as the biggest share,

468
00:13:33.717 --> 00:13:35.080
and no new data.

469
00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:37.280
Before switching on any AI,

470
00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:38.400
write

471
00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:39.500
the integration contract,

472
00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.320
in five lines:

473
00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:42.560
the data sent,

474
00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:44.140
the available model,

475
00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:45.300
the cost limit,

476
00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:46.760
the maximum time,

477
00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:49.180
and what happens when the AI fails.

478
00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:50.740
The last line is the one most

479
00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.160
often forgotten,

480
00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.780
and it's the one that keeps the

481
00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:55.540
bot useful even when the AI doesn't

482
00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.480
answer.

483
00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:57.980
Denise wrote the one for horario in

484
00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:00.120
five minutes, and on the failure line

485
00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:01.800
she put: without AI,

486
00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:03.380
the bot sends the spreadsheet row as

487
00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:04.220
it is.

488
00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:06.220
The cost and time values are examples;

489
00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:07.380
you set your own.

490
00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.180
And one firm rule:

491
00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:11.380
the message never goes straight to an

492
00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:13.320
agent like Codex.

493
00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:15.320
Whoever writes on Telegram can't make an

494
00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:17.500
agent act on your computer.

495
00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.440
The AI receives a short input,

496
00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:21.400
built by the program,

497
00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:22.800
and returns text.

498
00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:23.800
Pause the video,

499
00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.000
write your contract,

500
00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:26.160
and test in the chat that the

501
00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:28.340
summary keeps the one hundred reais.

502
00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:29.880
Before taking the bot anywhere,

503
00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:31.660
it's worth proving that it fails well.

504
00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:34.320
The kit comes with a self-test:

505
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.540
the bot runs fake messages against

506
00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.120
its own rules,

507
00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:41.177
with no token and no internet.

508
00:14:41.177 --> 00:14:42.577
It covers access,

509
00:14:42.577 --> 00:14:44.497
group, unknown command,

510
00:14:44.497 --> 00:14:46.977
the sum, and broken sales files.

511
00:14:46.977 --> 00:14:49.751
The command is python3 bot.py with the

512
00:14:49.751 --> 00:14:50.657
self test option,

513
00:14:50.657 --> 00:14:52.297
and the answer is a single line,

514
00:14:52.297 --> 00:14:55.577
starting with OK and mentioning eleven scenarios.

515
00:14:55.577 --> 00:14:57.137
If a long error shows up,

516
00:14:57.137 --> 00:14:58.457
some scenario failed.

517
00:14:58.457 --> 00:14:59.237
But watch out:

518
00:14:59.237 --> 00:15:01.037
the self-test doesn't

519
00:15:01.037 --> 00:15:03.017
prove that your bot talks to Telegram.

520
00:15:03.017 --> 00:15:04.817
It's simulated, and it goes in the

521
00:15:04.817 --> 00:15:06.537
log as simulated.

522
00:15:06.777 --> 00:15:09.257
Denise asked whether Lúcia's bot obeyed strangers.

523
00:15:09.257 --> 00:15:10.397
Lúcia

524
00:15:10.397 --> 00:15:12.477
showed the last line of the self-test

525
00:15:12.477 --> 00:15:14.577
and noted that the real test was

526
00:15:14.577 --> 00:15:16.017
still missing,

527
00:15:16.297 --> 00:15:19.297
with someone from outside the list.

528
00:15:19.297 --> 00:15:20.677
It's like a sound check before the

529
00:15:20.677 --> 00:15:22.997
parents' meeting: you test the microphone with

530
00:15:22.997 --> 00:15:23.717
the auditorium empty.

531
00:15:23.717 --> 00:15:25.397
On Telegram,

532
00:15:25.397 --> 00:15:26.617
four real tests are enough:

533
00:15:26.617 --> 00:15:28.697
your own status,

534
00:15:28.697 --> 00:15:30.957
any random sentence,

535
00:15:31.397 --> 00:15:33.317
a person who's not on the list,

536
00:15:33.317 --> 00:15:34.717
and the bot switched off.

537
00:15:34.717 --> 00:15:36.557
If the bot still replies while it's

538
00:15:36.557 --> 00:15:38.557
off, there's another copy running somewhere.

539
00:15:38.557 --> 00:15:40.427
Lúcia asked

540
00:15:40.427 --> 00:15:42.617
Denise to send relatorio.

541
00:15:42.617 --> 00:15:43.597
Nothing came back,

542
00:15:43.597 --> 00:15:45.497
as expected, and she wrote down:

543
00:15:45.497 --> 00:15:46.997
off the list,

544
00:15:46.997 --> 00:15:48.755
Telegram, no reply.

545
00:15:48.755 --> 00:15:50.255
And when something fails,

546
00:15:50.255 --> 00:15:52.275
the symptom tells you where to look.

547
00:15:52.275 --> 00:15:54.075
Don't switch the AI model,

548
00:15:54.075 --> 00:15:56.815
because status and relatorio don't even use

549
00:15:56.815 --> 00:15:57.735
AI.

550
00:15:57.735 --> 00:15:59.315
If only relatorio fails,

551
00:15:59.315 --> 00:16:01.635
the problem is in the sales file.

552
00:16:02.015 --> 00:16:03.695
Lúcia got the message that the file

553
00:16:03.695 --> 00:16:05.315
couldn't be validated,

554
00:16:05.335 --> 00:16:07.035
and found out she had deleted the

555
00:16:07.035 --> 00:16:07.755
header.

556
00:16:07.755 --> 00:16:09.175
If nothing replies,

557
00:16:09.175 --> 00:16:10.415
check the program,

558
00:16:10.415 --> 00:16:12.815
the token, the internet and the access

559
00:16:12.815 --> 00:16:13.755
list.

560
00:16:13.755 --> 00:16:15.075
On a network failure,

561
00:16:15.075 --> 00:16:16.895
the bot retries on its own.

562
00:16:16.895 --> 00:16:18.015
On a conflict,

563
00:16:18.015 --> 00:16:18.595
the four oh nine,

564
00:16:18.595 --> 00:16:20.235
or with the wrong token,

565
00:16:20.235 --> 00:16:21.135
the four oh one,

566
00:16:21.135 --> 00:16:22.735
it shuts itself down so you can

567
00:16:22.735 --> 00:16:23.935
investigate.

568
00:16:25.015 --> 00:16:26.735
The log shows the type of failure

569
00:16:26.735 --> 00:16:28.535
and the time,

570
00:16:28.535 --> 00:16:30.275
but it doesn't show the token or

571
00:16:30.275 --> 00:16:32.195
the text of the messages.

572
00:16:32.195 --> 00:16:33.935
Lúcia turned off the Wi-Fi on purpose,

573
00:16:33.935 --> 00:16:35.175
with the bot running.

574
00:16:35.175 --> 00:16:37.695
The terminal showed retry warnings,

575
00:16:37.695 --> 00:16:39.415
each one waiting twice as long as

576
00:16:39.415 --> 00:16:41.135
the last, and the bot came back

577
00:16:41.135 --> 00:16:43.515
on its own when the network returned.

578
00:16:43.515 --> 00:16:45.875
Pause the video and sound-check your bot.

579
00:16:45.875 --> 00:16:47.275
Run the self-test,

580
00:16:47.275 --> 00:16:48.575
start the bot,

581
00:16:48.575 --> 00:16:50.655
send status and any sentence,

582
00:16:50.655 --> 00:16:52.332
ask someone off the list to send

583
00:16:52.332 --> 00:16:54.052
relatorio and, finally,

584
00:16:54.052 --> 00:16:56.512
stop it and confirm the silence.

585
00:16:57.072 --> 00:16:59.712
Mark each line as simulated or Telegram.

586
00:16:59.712 --> 00:17:00.992
With no one to help,

587
00:17:00.992 --> 00:17:02.612
write not tested:

588
00:17:02.612 --> 00:17:05.012
an honest log is worth more.

589
00:17:05.072 --> 00:17:06.512
Let's put it all together.

590
00:17:06.512 --> 00:17:08.612
Telegram carries messages back and forth,

591
00:17:08.612 --> 00:17:10.032
and the one that decides is your

592
00:17:10.032 --> 00:17:11.052
program,

593
00:17:11.052 --> 00:17:13.192
which accepts only known commands.

594
00:17:13.192 --> 00:17:14.662
The bot token lives only in the

595
00:17:14.662 --> 00:17:16.272
dot env, protected,

596
00:17:16.472 --> 00:17:18.432
and if it leaks you revoke and

597
00:17:18.432 --> 00:17:19.572
replace it.

598
00:17:19.572 --> 00:17:21.352
The access list says who the bot

599
00:17:21.352 --> 00:17:22.912
serves, by number,

600
00:17:22.912 --> 00:17:24.092
not by name.

601
00:17:24.092 --> 00:17:26.292
You start the bot with long polling,

602
00:17:26.292 --> 00:17:27.872
check the total against the file,

603
00:17:27.872 --> 00:17:30.172
and keep just one copy running.

604
00:17:30.272 --> 00:17:32.532
AI comes in at one step,

605
00:17:32.532 --> 00:17:34.532
after the base is tested,

606
00:17:34.532 --> 00:17:36.572
with a five-line contract and the number

607
00:17:36.572 --> 00:17:37.972
left untouched.

608
00:17:37.972 --> 00:17:40.012
And you test before you trust,

609
00:17:40.012 --> 00:17:42.172
separating what was simulated from what was

610
00:17:42.172 --> 00:17:42.892
real.

611
00:17:42.892 --> 00:17:44.552
When you have about thirty minutes,

612
00:17:44.552 --> 00:17:45.412
do the module lab,

613
00:17:45.412 --> 00:17:47.632
in the supplementary material.

614
00:17:47.632 --> 00:17:48.792
In the next module,

615
00:17:48.792 --> 00:17:51.072
VPS from scratch and

616
00:17:51.652 --> 00:17:53.692
twenty-four seven operation:

617
00:17:53.752 --> 00:17:55.772
the bot running all day long,

618
00:17:55.772 --> 00:17:58.672
without depending on your computer.

619
00:17:58.892 --> 00:17:59.549
See you there.
